{"family":"qb-x11-me-f2","course":"EXT1","year":11,"topic":"ME-F2","questions":[{"id":"X11-F2-001(ii)","group":"X11-F2-001","label":"(ii)","dp":"F2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Two factors give two equations","prompt":"The polynomial $P(x)=x^{3}+ax^{2}+bx-6$ is divisible by $(x-1)$ and by $(x+2)$.\n\nFactorise $P(x)$ fully.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"(x-1)*(x+2)*(x+3)"},"answerPrefix":"P(x) =","hints":["Two factors are known.","Match the constant term.","Check by expanding."],"steps":[{"h":"Third factor","d":"Constant: $(-1)(2)c=-6\\Rightarrow c=3$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"(x-1)*(x+2)*(x-3)","why":"Sign of the third root: product of roots is 6."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"(x − 1)(x + 2)(x + 3)","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-002","group":"X11-F2-002","dp":"F2.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Remainder on division by a quadratic","prompt":"Find the remainder when $x^{5}-3x^{2}+1$ is divided by $x^{2}-1$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x-2"},"answerPrefix":"R(x) =","hints":["The remainder has degree at most 1.","Substitute x = ±1.","Solve for a and b."],"steps":[{"h":"Form","d":"$P(x)=(x^{2}-1)Q(x)+ax+b$"},{"h":"Substitute","d":"$P(1)=-1=a+b$, $P(-1)=-3=-a+b$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$a=1$, $b=-2$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"-1","why":"Divided by x − 1 only."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Remainder form ax + b","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Two equations","line":"a+b = -1"},{"marks":1,"point":"x − 2","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-003(i)","group":"X11-F2-003","label":"(i)","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Symmetric functions of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-4x^{2}+2x+5=0$ are $\\alpha$, $\\beta$ and $\\gamma$. Find:\n\n$\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}+\\gamma^{2}$","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":12},"hints":["Σα = −b/a.","Σαβ = c/a.","Square the sum."],"steps":[{"h":"Sums","d":"$\\sum\\alpha=4$, $\\sum\\alpha\\beta=2$"},{"h":"Identity","d":"$16-2(2)=12$"}],"traps":[{"value":20,"why":"Added 2Σαβ."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Uses (Σα)² − 2Σαβ","line":"4^2-2*2"},{"marks":1,"point":"12","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-003(ii)","group":"X11-F2-003","label":"(ii)","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Symmetric functions of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-4x^{2}+2x+5=0$ are $\\alpha$, $\\beta$ and $\\gamma$. Find:\n\n$\\dfrac1\\alpha+\\dfrac1\\beta+\\dfrac1\\gamma$","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-0.4},"hints":["Common denominator αβγ.","αβγ = −d/a.","Divide."],"steps":[{"h":"Combine","d":"$\\dfrac{\\sum\\alpha\\beta}{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma}=\\dfrac{2}{-5}$"}],"traps":[{"value":0.4,"why":"αβγ = −d/a = −5.","expr":"2/5"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−2/5","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-007","group":"X11-F2-007","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Equation with squared roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{2}-3x+1=0$ are $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Find a quadratic equation with roots $\\alpha^{2}$ and $\\beta^{2}$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"x^2-7*x+1","rhs":"0"},"hints":["α + β = 3, αβ = 1.","Find the new sum and product.","x² − (sum)x + product = 0."],"steps":[{"h":"New sum","d":"$\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}=9-2=7$"},{"h":"New product","d":"$(\\alpha\\beta)^{2}=1$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"x^2-9*x+1 = 0","why":"Used (α + β)² as α² + β²."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Sum 7 and product 1","line":"3^2-2*1"},{"marks":1,"point":"x² − 7x + 1 = 0","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-010","group":"X11-F2-010","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Cubic with surd roots","prompt":"Find the monic cubic with roots $2$, $1+\\sqrt3$ and $1-\\sqrt3$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x^3-4*x^2+2*x+4"},"answerPrefix":"P(x) =","hints":["Multiply the surd pair first.","Difference of squares.","Then multiply by x − 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Pair","d":"$(x-1)^{2}-3=x^{2}-2x-2$"},{"h":"Multiply","d":"$(x-2)(x^{2}-2x-2)$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"x^3-4*x^2+2*x-4","why":"Sign of the constant: (−2)(−2) = 4."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"x² − 2x − 2","line":"x^2-2*x-2"},{"marks":1,"point":"Expanded cubic","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-012","group":"X11-F2-012","dp":"F2.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":3,"title":"Combining two remainders","prompt":"When $P(x)$ is divided by $(x-1)$ the remainder is $3$, and when divided by $(x+2)$ the remainder is $-6$. Find the remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $(x-1)(x+2)$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"3*x"},"answerPrefix":"R(x) =","hints":["Degree of the remainder is at most 1.","Substitute x = 1 and −2.","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Form","d":"$P=(x-1)(x+2)Q+ax+b$"},{"h":"Equations","d":"$a+b=3$, $-2a+b=-6$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$a=3$, $b=0$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"-3","why":"Added the remainders."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Remainder ax + b","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Two equations","line":"a+b = 3"},{"marks":1,"point":"3x","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-019","group":"X11-F2-019","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Reciprocal roots","prompt":"The roots of $2x^{3}-5x^{2}+3x-7=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find a cubic equation with integer coefficients whose roots are $\\dfrac1\\alpha,\\dfrac1\\beta,\\dfrac1\\gamma$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"7*x^3-3*x^2+5*x-2","rhs":"0"},"hints":["If α is a root, 1/α is a root of P(1/x) = 0.","Multiply by x³.","Reverse the coefficients."],"steps":[{"h":"Substitute","d":"$x\\to\\tfrac1x$: $\\tfrac{2}{x^{3}}-\\tfrac{5}{x^{2}}+\\tfrac3x-7=0$"},{"h":"Clear","d":"$7x^{3}-3x^{2}+5x-2=0$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"-7*x^3+5*x^2-3*x+2 = 0","why":"Reversed the coefficients but kept the original signs pattern wrongly."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Replaces x by 1/x","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct cubic","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-027","group":"X11-F2-027","dp":"F2.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Quick remainder","prompt":"Find the remainder when $P(x)=x^{3}-2x^{2}+4$ is divided by $x-2$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":4},"hints":["Use the remainder theorem.","Evaluate P(2).","Simplify."],"steps":[{"h":"Remainder theorem","d":"$P(2)=8-8+4$"}],"traps":[{"value":20,"why":"Evaluated P(−2) with the wrong sign."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"4","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-028","group":"X11-F2-028","dp":"F2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Unknown coefficient from a factor","prompt":"Find $k$ given that $x+1$ is a factor of $2x^{3}+kx^{2}-3x+4$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-5},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["x + 1 is a factor so P(−1) = 0.","Substitute carefully.","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Factor theorem","d":"$P(-1)=-2+k+3+4=0$"}],"traps":[{"value":5,"why":"Sign slip in k + 5 = 0."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"P(−1) = 0","line":"k+5 = 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"k = −5","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-029","group":"X11-F2-029","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Sum of squares of three roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-2x^{2}-5x+6=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}+\\gamma^{2}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":14},"hints":["Σα = −b/a.","Σαβ = c/a.","Use (Σα)² − 2Σαβ."],"steps":[{"h":"Sums","d":"$\\sum\\alpha=2$, $\\sum\\alpha\\beta=-5$"},{"h":"Identity","d":"$4-2(-5)=14$"}],"traps":[{"value":-6,"why":"Sign of Σαβ."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Σα and Σαβ","line":"2^2-2*(-5)"},{"marks":1,"point":"14","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-032","group":"X11-F2-032","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Reciprocal sum of roots","prompt":"The roots of $2x^{3}-3x^{2}+4x-5=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\dfrac1\\alpha+\\dfrac1\\beta+\\dfrac1\\gamma$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.8},"hints":["Combine over αβγ.","Σαβ = c/a.","αβγ = −d/a."],"steps":[{"h":"Values","d":"$\\sum\\alpha\\beta=2$, $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=\\tfrac52$"},{"h":"Divide","d":"$\\tfrac{2}{5/2}=\\tfrac45$"}],"traps":[{"value":-0.8,"why":"αβγ = −d/a = +5/2.","expr":"-4/5"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Σαβ = 2, αβγ = 5/2","line":"2/(5/2)"},{"marks":1,"point":"4/5","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-033","group":"X11-F2-033","dp":"F2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":3,"title":"Solving a cubic from one root","prompt":"Solve $2x^{3}-x^{2}-5x-2=0$.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[2,-0.5,-1]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Test small integers.","Divide by the factor.","Factorise the quadratic."],"steps":[{"h":"Root","d":"$P(2)=16-4-10-2=0$"},{"h":"Divide","d":"$(x-2)(2x^{2}+3x+1)$"},{"h":"Factor","d":"$(x-2)(2x+1)(x+1)$"}],"traps":[{"values":[2,"1/2",1],"why":"Signs of the remaining roots."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Finds x = 2","line":"(x-2)*(2*x^2+3*x+1) = 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"Factorises the quadratic","line":"(x-2)*(2*x+1)*(x+1) = 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"All roots","answer":true}],"stepcheck":{"kind":"equation","variable":"x","solutions":[2,-0.5,-1]}},{"id":"X11-F2-041","group":"X11-F2-041","dp":"F2.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Remainder on division by a quadratic","prompt":"Find the remainder when $P(x)=x^{4}+x+1$ is divided by $x^{2}-x$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"2*x+1"},"answerPrefix":"R(x) =","hints":["x² − x = x(x − 1).","The remainder is ax + b.","Substitute the roots."],"steps":[{"h":"Form","d":"$P(x)=x(x-1)Q(x)+ax+b$"},{"h":"Substitute","d":"$P(0)=1=b$, $P(1)=3=a+b$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"3","why":"Divided by x − 1 only."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Uses x = 0 and x = 1","line":"a+b = 3"},{"marks":1,"point":"2x + 1","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-042","group":"X11-F2-042","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Sum of cubes of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{2}-4x+1=0$ are $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Find $\\alpha^{3}+\\beta^{3}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":52},"hints":["α + β = 4, αβ = 1.","Expand (α + β)³.","Rearrange."],"steps":[{"h":"Identity","d":"$(\\alpha+\\beta)^{3}-3\\alpha\\beta(\\alpha+\\beta)=64-12$"}],"traps":[{"value":64,"why":"Forgot the −3αβ(α + β) term."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Uses the cube identity","line":"4^3-3*1*4"},{"marks":1,"point":"52","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-045","group":"X11-F2-045","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Product of shifted roots","prompt":"The roots of $P(x)=x^{3}+2x^{2}-3x-1$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $(\\alpha+1)(\\beta+1)(\\gamma+1)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-3},"hints":["P(x) = (x − α)(x − β)(x − γ).","Substitute x = −1.","Three minus signs."],"steps":[{"h":"Factored form","d":"$P(-1)=(-1-\\alpha)(-1-\\beta)(-1-\\gamma)=-(\\alpha+1)(\\beta+1)(\\gamma+1)$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$P(-1)=-1+2+3-1=3$"}],"traps":[{"value":3,"why":"Sign from the three negative factors."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Links to P(−1)","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"−3","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-048","group":"X11-F2-048","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Doubling every root","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-3x+1=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find a monic cubic with roots $2\\alpha,2\\beta,2\\gamma$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"x^3-12*x+8","rhs":"0"},"hints":["If y = 2x then x = y/2.","Substitute into the cubic.","Clear fractions."],"steps":[{"h":"Substitute","d":"Replace $x$ by $\\tfrac x2$: $\\tfrac{x^{3}}{8}-\\tfrac{3x}{2}+1=0$"},{"h":"Clear","d":"Multiply by $8$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"x^3-6*x+2 = 0","why":"Substituted 2x instead of x/2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Substitutes x/2","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct cubic","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-050","group":"X11-F2-050","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Integer roots of a cubic","prompt":"Find all roots of $x^{3}-2x^{2}-5x+6=0$.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[1,-2,3]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Integer roots divide 6.","Test x = 1.","Factorise the quadratic."],"steps":[{"h":"Try divisors of 6","d":"$P(1)=0$"},{"h":"Factor","d":"$(x-1)(x^{2}-x-6)=(x-1)(x-3)(x+2)$"}],"traps":[{"values":[-1,2,-3],"why":"Signs of the roots."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Finds a root and divides","line":"(x-1)*(x^2-x-6) = 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"All roots","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-052","group":"X11-F2-052","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Negative sum of squares","prompt":"The roots of $2x^{3}-x^{2}+3x-4=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}+\\gamma^{2}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-2.75},"hints":["Divide by the leading coefficient.","(Σα)² − 2Σαβ.","A negative answer means some roots are not real."],"steps":[{"h":"Sums","d":"$\\sum\\alpha=\\tfrac12$, $\\sum\\alpha\\beta=\\tfrac32$"},{"h":"Identity","d":"$\\tfrac14-3$"}],"traps":[{"value":3.25,"why":"Added 2Σαβ.","expr":"13/4"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Both sums","line":"1/4-3"},{"marks":1,"point":"−11/4","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-054","group":"X11-F2-054","dp":"F2.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"A huge power divided by a quadratic","prompt":"Find the remainder when $x^{100}$ is divided by $x^{2}-1$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":1},"hints":["Remainder is ax + b.","Substitute x = ±1.","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Form","d":"$x^{100}=(x^{2}-1)Q(x)+ax+b$"},{"h":"Substitute","d":"$a+b=1$, $-a+b=1$: $a=0$, $b=1$"}],"traps":[{"value":0,"why":"1¹⁰⁰ = 1, not 0."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Two equations","line":"a+b = 1"},{"marks":1,"point":"1","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-055","group":"X11-F2-055","dp":"F2.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Sum of roots of a quartic","prompt":"Find the sum of the roots of $x^{4}-3x^{3}+2x-5=0$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":3},"hints":["Sum of roots = −b/a.","b = −3.","a = 1."],"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$-\\tfrac ba=3$"}],"traps":[{"value":-3,"why":"Sum is −b/a."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"3","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-058","group":"X11-F2-058","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Shifting both roots by one","prompt":"The roots of $x^{2}+3x-1=0$ are $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Find a quadratic with roots $\\alpha+1$ and $\\beta+1$.","answerType":"equation","answer":{"lhs":"x^2+x-3","rhs":"0"},"hints":["If y = x + 1 then x = y − 1.","Substitute.","Expand."],"steps":[{"h":"Substitute","d":"Replace $x$ by $x-1$: $(x-1)^{2}+3(x-1)-1$"}],"traps":[{"eq":"x^2+5*x+3 = 0","why":"Substituted x + 1."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Substitutes x − 1","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct quadratic","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-060","group":"X11-F2-060","dp":"F2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"A cubic inequality from a factorisation","prompt":"Solve $x^{3}-6x^{2}+11x-6\\ge0$.","answerType":"interval","answer":{"region":"1 <= x <= 2 or x >= 3","variable":"x"},"hints":["Try x = 1.","Factorise fully.","Sign diagram."],"steps":[{"h":"Factor","d":"$(x-1)(x-2)(x-3)$"},{"h":"Signs","d":"$1\\le x\\le2$ or $x\\ge3$"}],"traps":[{"region":"x <= 1 or 2 <= x <= 3","why":"That is where the cubic is ≤ 0."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Factorises","line":"(x-1)*(x-2)*(x-3) >= 0"},{"marks":1,"point":"Correct solution","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-061","group":"X11-F2-061","dp":"F2.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Remainder fixes a coefficient","prompt":"When $P(x)=x^{3}+kx-4$ is divided by $x-2$, the remainder is $10$. Find $k$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":3},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Remainder is P(2).","Substitute.","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Remainder theorem","d":"$8+2k-4=10$"}],"traps":[{"value":7,"why":"Forgot the −4."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"k = 3","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-062","group":"X11-F2-062","dp":"F2.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Product of roots taken two at a time","prompt":"The roots of $2x^{3}-5x^{2}+7x-1=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":3.5},"hints":["Σαβ = c/a.","c = 7.","a = 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\tfrac ca$"}],"traps":[{"value":-3.5,"why":"Pairs sum is +c/a.","expr":"-7/2"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"7/2","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-063","group":"X11-F2-063","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Reciprocals of the roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-4x^{2}+6x-3=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\dfrac1\\alpha+\\dfrac1\\beta+\\dfrac1\\gamma$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":2},"hints":["Common denominator.","Σαβ = 6.","αβγ = 3."],"steps":[{"h":"Combine","d":"$\\dfrac{\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha}{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma}$"},{"h":"Values","d":"$\\tfrac63$"}],"traps":[{"value":1.3333333333333333,"why":"That uses Σα.","expr":"4/3"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Combined fraction","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"2","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-064","group":"X11-F2-064","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Roots in arithmetic progression","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-9x^{2}+23x-15=0$ form an arithmetic sequence. Find them.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[1,3,5]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Write roots a − d, a, a + d.","Sum = 9.","Divide by x − 3."],"steps":[{"h":"Middle root","d":"$(a-d)+a+(a+d)=9\\Rightarrow a=3$"},{"h":"Factor","d":"$(x-3)(x^{2}-6x+5)$"}],"traps":[{"values":[3],"why":"Find the other two."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Middle root 3","line":"x = 3"},{"marks":1,"point":"All roots","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-067","group":"X11-F2-067","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Sum of squares of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-2x^{2}-5x+6=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}+\\gamma^{2}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":14},"hints":["Σα = 2.","Σαβ = −5.","Square and subtract."],"steps":[{"h":"Identity","d":"$(\\Sigma\\alpha)^{2}-2\\Sigma\\alpha\\beta$"},{"h":"Values","d":"$4+10$"}],"traps":[{"value":-6,"why":"Σαβ = −5, so −2Σαβ = +10."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Uses the identity","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"14","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-070","group":"X11-F2-070","dp":"F2.2a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Product of roots of a quartic","prompt":"Find the product of the roots of $3x^{4}-x^{3}+2x-12=0$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-4},"hints":["Quartic product is e/a.","e = −12.","a = 3."],"steps":[{"h":"Formula","d":"$\\tfrac ea=\\tfrac{-12}{3}$"}],"traps":[{"value":4,"why":"For an even degree the product is +e/a."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−4","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-071","group":"X11-F2-071","dp":"F2.1a","authored":1,"level":1,"marks":1,"title":"Divide a cubic by a linear factor","prompt":"Divide $x^{3}-5x^{2}+2x+8$ by $x-2$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x^2-3*x-4"},"answerPrefix":"Quotient =","hints":["Divide x³ by x.","Multiply and subtract.","Repeat."],"steps":[{"h":"Long division","d":"Remainder $0$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"x^2-7*x+16","why":"Divided by x + 2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct quotient","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-072","group":"X11-F2-072","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Roots in geometric progression","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-7x^{2}+14x-8=0$ are in geometric progression. Find them.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[1,2,4]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Roots a/r, a, ar.","Product = 8.","Divide by x − 2."],"steps":[{"h":"Product","d":"$\\tfrac ar\\cdot a\\cdot ar=a^{3}=8\\Rightarrow a=2$"},{"h":"Factor","d":"$(x-2)(x^{2}-5x+4)$"}],"traps":[{"values":[2],"why":"Find the other two."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Middle root 2","line":"x = 2"},{"marks":1,"point":"All roots","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-074","group":"X11-F2-074","dp":"F2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Remainder from a large power","prompt":"Find the remainder when $x^{50}+2x-1$ is divided by $x+1$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":-2},"hints":["Substitute x = −1.","Even power is 1.","Add."],"steps":[{"h":"Remainder theorem","d":"$1-2-1$"}],"traps":[{"value":0,"why":"(−1)⁵⁰ = 1."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"−2","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-075","group":"X11-F2-075","dp":"F2.1b","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Multiple root condition","prompt":"$P(x)=x^{3}-3x+k$ has a double root. Find the possible values of $k$.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[2,-2]},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["A double root is also a root of P′.","Solve P′ = 0.","Substitute into P."],"steps":[{"h":"Derivative","d":"$P'(x)=3x^{2}-3=0\\Rightarrow x=\\pm1$"},{"h":"Root","d":"$P(\\pm1)=0$"}],"traps":[{"values":[2],"why":"x = −1 gives k = −2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Double root at ±1","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"k = ±2","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-076","group":"X11-F2-076","dp":"F2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Remainder of a division as a polynomial","prompt":"Find the remainder when $x^{4}+2x^{3}-x+5$ is divided by $x^{2}+1$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"-3*x+6"},"answerPrefix":"Remainder =","hints":["Long division or x² = −1.","Reduce each power.","Collect."],"steps":[{"h":"Reduce","d":"$x^{2}=-1$: $x^{4}=1$, $x^{3}=-x$"},{"h":"Substitute","d":"$1-2x-x+5$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"x+6","why":"x³ = −x, so 2x³ = −2x."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Uses x² = −1 or long division","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"−3x + 6","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-084","group":"X11-F2-084","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Quartic with two known roots","prompt":"$P(x)=x^{4}-x^{3}-7x^{2}+x+6$ has roots $1$ and $-1$. Find the other roots.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[-2,3]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Divide by x² − 1.","Factor the quotient.","Read the roots."],"steps":[{"h":"Divide","d":"$P(x)=(x^{2}-1)(x^{2}-x-6)$"},{"h":"Factor","d":"$(x-3)(x+2)$"}],"traps":[{"values":[3],"why":"x + 2 is also a factor."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Quotient x² − x − 6","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Both roots","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-085","group":"X11-F2-085","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Cubic with a given sum and product of roots","prompt":"A monic cubic has roots $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$ with $\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=4$, $\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha=1$ and $\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=-6$. Write the cubic.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"x^3-4*x^2+x+6"},"answerPrefix":"P(x) =","hints":["Signs alternate.","−Σα for x².","−αβγ constant."],"steps":[{"h":"Coefficients","d":"$x^{3}-(\\Sigma)x^{2}+(\\Sigma\\alpha\\beta)x-\\alpha\\beta\\gamma$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"x^3+4*x^2+x-6","why":"Alternate the signs."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Correct cubic","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-087","group":"X11-F2-087","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Sum of cubes of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{2}-3x+1=0$ are $\\alpha$ and $\\beta$. Find $\\alpha^{3}+\\beta^{3}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":18},"hints":["α + β = 3, αβ = 1.","Cube identity.","Compute."],"steps":[{"h":"Identity","d":"$(\\alpha+\\beta)^{3}-3\\alpha\\beta(\\alpha+\\beta)$"},{"h":"Values","d":"$27-9$"}],"traps":[{"value":27,"why":"Subtract 3αβ(α + β)."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Identity","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"18","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-090","group":"X11-F2-090","dp":"F2.2a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":2,"title":"Integer root search","prompt":"Find all real roots of $x^{3}+x^{2}-5x+3=0$.","answerType":"set","answer":{"values":[1,-3]},"answerPrefix":"x =","hints":["Try factors of 3.","Divide.","Factor the quadratic."],"steps":[{"h":"Test","d":"$P(1)=0$"},{"h":"Factor","d":"$(x-1)(x^{2}+2x-3)=(x-1)^{2}(x+3)$"}],"traps":[{"values":[1],"why":"x = −3 also."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Finds x = 1","line":"x = 1"},{"marks":1,"point":"All roots","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-097","group":"X11-F2-097","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Sum of reciprocals of squares of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{2}-5x+2=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta$. Find $\\dfrac1{\\alpha^{2}}+\\dfrac1{\\beta^{2}}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":5.25},"hints":["Common denominator.","α² + β² = (α + β)² − 2αβ.","Divide by 4."],"steps":[{"h":"Combine","d":"$\\dfrac{\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}}{(\\alpha\\beta)^{2}}$"},{"h":"Values","d":"$\\dfrac{25-4}{4}$"}],"traps":[{"value":6.25,"why":"α² + β² = 25 − 4.","expr":"25/4"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Combined fraction","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"21/4","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-106","group":"X11-F2-106","dp":"F2.2b","authored":5,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Sum of fourth powers of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{2}-x-1=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta$. Find $\\alpha^{4}+\\beta^{4}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":7},"hints":["α + β = 1, αβ = −1.","Square sums twice.","Subtract."],"steps":[{"h":"Squares","d":"$\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2}=1+2=3$"},{"h":"Fourth powers","d":"$(\\alpha^{2}+\\beta^{2})^{2}-2(\\alpha\\beta)^{2}=9-2$"}],"traps":[{"value":9,"why":"Subtract 2(αβ)²."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Sum of squares 3","line":"3"},{"marks":1,"point":"7","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-108","group":"X11-F2-108","dp":"F2.1a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Remainder on division by a quadratic","prompt":"When $P(x)$ is divided by $x-1$ the remainder is $3$, and when divided by $x+2$ the remainder is $-6$. Find the remainder when $P(x)$ is divided by $(x-1)(x+2)$.","answerType":"expression","answer":{"expr":"3*x"},"answerPrefix":"R(x) =","hints":["Remainder is linear.","Substitute x = 1 and −2.","Solve simultaneously."],"steps":[{"h":"Form","d":"$P(x)=(x-1)(x+2)Q(x)+ax+b$"},{"h":"Equations","d":"$a+b=3$, $-2a+b=-6$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$a=3$, $b=0$"}],"traps":[{"expr":"3*x+0*x+3","why":"Solve both equations."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Linear remainder form","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Two equations","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"3x","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-119","group":"X11-F2-119","dp":"F2.2b","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":2,"title":"Product of pairwise sums of roots","prompt":"The roots of $P(x)=x^{3}-4x^{2}+2x-1=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $(\\alpha+\\beta)(\\beta+\\gamma)(\\gamma+\\alpha)$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":7},"hints":["Σα = 4.","Each pair sum is 4 minus the third root.","Evaluate P(4)."],"steps":[{"h":"Rewrite","d":"$\\alpha+\\beta=4-\\gamma$, etc."},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$(4-\\alpha)(4-\\beta)(4-\\gamma)=P(4)=7$"}],"traps":[{"value":-7,"why":"P(4) equals (4 − α)(4 − β)(4 − γ) for a monic cubic."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Rewrite with the sum","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"7","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-120","group":"X11-F2-120","dp":"F2.2b","authored":5,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Roots in arithmetic progression","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-6x^{2}+kx-6=0$ are in arithmetic progression. Find the roots and $k$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":11},"answerPrefix":"k =","hints":["Write the roots as a − d, a, a + d.","Sum of roots gives a.","Use the product."],"steps":[{"h":"Sum","d":"$3a=6\\Rightarrow a=2$"},{"h":"Product","d":"$2(4-d^{2})=6\\Rightarrow d=\\pm1$"},{"h":"k","d":"$\\sum\\alpha\\beta=2+3+6$"}],"traps":[{"value":6,"why":"k is the sum of pairwise products."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Middle root 2","line":"2"},{"marks":1,"point":"Roots 1 2 3","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"k = 11","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-121","group":"X11-F2-121","dp":"F2.1a","authored":2,"level":2,"marks":1,"title":"Remainder theorem","prompt":"Find the remainder when $x^{3}-2x+5$ is divided by $x+2$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":1},"hints":["Remainder is P(−2).","Substitute.","Simplify."],"steps":[{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$P(-2)=-8+4+5$"}],"traps":[{"value":9,"why":"Substitute x = −2."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"1","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-134","group":"X11-F2-134","dp":"F2.1a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Coefficient from a remainder","prompt":"When $P(x)=x^{4}-3x^{3}+ax-6$ is divided by $x-2$ the remainder is $4$. Find $a$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":9},"answerPrefix":"a =","hints":["P(2) = 4.","Simplify.","Solve."],"steps":[{"h":"Remainder theorem","d":"$16-24+2a-6=4$"},{"h":"Solve","d":"$2a=18$"}],"traps":[{"value":7,"why":"−8 − 6 = −14, so 2a = 18."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"P(2) = 4","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"a = 9","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-136","group":"X11-F2-136","dp":"F2.2a","authored":3,"level":3,"marks":2,"title":"Sum of reciprocals of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}+2x^{2}-3x+5=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\dfrac1\\alpha+\\dfrac1\\beta+\\dfrac1\\gamma$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":0.6},"hints":["Common denominator.","Σαβ = −3.","αβγ = −5."],"steps":[{"h":"Combine","d":"$\\dfrac{\\alpha\\beta+\\beta\\gamma+\\gamma\\alpha}{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma}$"},{"h":"Vieta","d":"$\\dfrac{-3}{-5}$"}],"traps":[{"value":-0.6,"why":"αβγ = −5.","expr":"-3/5"}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Combined fraction","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"3/5","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-137","group":"X11-F2-137","dp":"F2.2a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"A mixed symmetric sum of roots","prompt":"For the roots of $x^{3}+2x^{2}-3x+5=0$, find $\\alpha^{2}\\beta+\\alpha\\beta^{2}+\\beta^{2}\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma^{2}+\\gamma^{2}\\alpha+\\gamma\\alpha^{2}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":21},"hints":["Expand Σα·Σαβ.","It includes 3αβγ.","Subtract."],"steps":[{"h":"Identity","d":"$\\left(\\sum\\alpha\\right)\\left(\\sum\\alpha\\beta\\right)-3\\alpha\\beta\\gamma$"},{"h":"Values","d":"$(-2)(-3)-3(-5)$"},{"h":"Evaluate","d":"$21$"}],"traps":[{"value":6,"why":"Subtract 3αβγ = −15."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Identity","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Values","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"21","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-147","group":"X11-F2-147","dp":"F2.2a","authored":5,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Sum of cubes of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-2x^{2}-x+3=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\alpha^{3}+\\beta^{3}+\\gamma^{3}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":5},"hints":["Each root satisfies the cubic.","Sum over roots.","Need Σα²."],"steps":[{"h":"Sums","d":"$\\sum\\alpha=2$, $\\sum\\alpha^{2}=4+2=6$"},{"h":"Equation","d":"$\\alpha^{3}=2\\alpha^{2}+\\alpha-3$"},{"h":"Add","d":"$2(6)+2-9$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Σα²,'?'"},{"marks":1,"point":"Uses the equation","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"5","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-156","group":"X11-F2-156","dp":"F2.2a","authored":4,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Sum of squares of reciprocals of roots","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-3x^{2}+4x-2=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Find $\\dfrac1{\\alpha^{2}}+\\dfrac1{\\beta^{2}}+\\dfrac1{\\gamma^{2}}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":1},"hints":["Σ1/α = Σαβ/αβγ.","Σ1/(αβ) = Σα/αβγ.","Square and subtract."],"steps":[{"h":"Reciprocal sums","d":"$\\sum\\tfrac1\\alpha=\\tfrac42=2$, $\\sum\\tfrac1{\\alpha\\beta}=\\tfrac32$"},{"h":"Identity","d":"$2^{2}-2\\cdot\\tfrac32$"}],"traps":[],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"Σ1/α","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"Σ1/(αβ)","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"1","answer":true}]},{"id":"X11-F2-E02(ii)","group":"X11-F2-E02","label":"(ii)","dp":"F2.2a","authored":6,"level":4,"marks":3,"title":"Fifth powers of roots without solving","prompt":"The roots of $x^{3}-x-1=0$ are $\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma$. Let $S_n=\\alpha^{n}+\\beta^{n}+\\gamma^{n}$.\n\nHence find $\\alpha^{5}+\\beta^{5}+\\gamma^{5}$.","answerType":"numeric","answer":{"value":5},"hints":["S₂ = (Σα)² − 2Σαβ.","Use the recurrence twice.","Keep track of indices."],"steps":[{"h":"Start values","d":"$S_0=3$, $S_1=0$, $S_2=0-2(-1)=2$"},{"h":"Recur","d":"$S_3=S_1+S_0=3$, $S_4=S_2+S_1=2$"},{"h":"Answer","d":"$S_5=S_3+S_2=5$"}],"traps":[{"value":3,"why":"That is S₃."}],"criteria":[{"marks":1,"point":"S₀, S₁, S₂","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"S₃ = 3, S₄ = 2","manual":true},{"marks":1,"point":"5","answer":true}]}]}
